H.I.V. stands for ` Human Immuno-deficiency Virus` .
H.I.V. attacks the immune system of the body .
Immune system is such a system of arrangement in our body that saves us from infection .
"Immune system identifies the disease-carrier or ` external invaders`NNS like virus , bacteria , etc and kills them ."
"H.I.V. is a virus which attacks the immune system , specially CD-4 cells and destroys them ."
CD-4 cells help protect the body from different diseases .
What happens when a person gets infected with the H.I.V. .
By entering into CD-4 cells the HIV increases its number very fast by reproducing and during this new viruses gets born in the cells .
With this the CD-4 cells get divided .
With the division in the CD-4 cells many viruses enter into the blood-circulation .
"After this the H.I.V. attacks other CD-4 cells , and this process is repeated again and again ."
H.I.V. destroys most of the CD-4 cells and thus the immune system of infected person gets destroyed .
"H.I.V. test is easy , safe and available at public health centres ."
