Researchers from Chattrapati Shahu Ji Maharaj Medical University has discovered an indigenous technique for the test of cervical -LRB- passage forming the lower end of the womb -RRB- cancer .
It can be used to diagnose cervical cancer in its initial stage .
"According to researchers , this new technique can be used for the primary testing ."
According to researchers this test does not require any special equipment .
This technique is also used in the primary health centres .
"To devise this technique , researchers tested 328 women for acetic acid , lugol ` s iodine and Pap smear and found that there are indication of cervix cancer in 83 % women when tested with Pap smear ."
Out of which cancer was confirmed in 98.3 % .
In the acetic acid test there were indication of cancer in 55.5 % out of which 71.39 have confirmed it .
Whereas in the lugol ` s iodine test there were indication of cancer in 86.84 % out of which 48.3 % have confirmed cancer .
"Even though the symptoms of cervical cancer are found present in general tests , it must get through the histo pathological test for confirmation ."
"Once pey to the end of the neck-line passage at the womb -LRB- cervix -RRB- cancer , 70 % of the women reach hospital when the cancer is in its third stage ."
"After getting treatment at this stage , only 34.3 % women are able to survive for next five years ."
