Talk to your doctor about strategies for alleviating any discomfort.
"When your body is going through physical changes that may be completely new to you, it isn't always easy to talk to your health care provider."
"Maybe you're wondering whether you can have sex or what to do about hemorrhoids or constipation, or maybe you're feeling a great deal of anxiety about the delivery."
"You might feel embarrassed to ask these or other questions, but it's important to do so - your health care provider has probably heard them all before."
"Keep a running list of questions between your appointments, and take that list with you to each visit."
"The risk of malaria, for those travelling to affected areas is significant, and so it is very important to take precautions to prevent it."
"Each year, around 2,000 travellers return to the UK with malaria, with the majority having acquired it in Africa."
